dom use", "Medications include oral contraceptives and NSAIDs"], "excluded_candidates": ["Musculoskeletal injury: less likely due to systemic hypotension and fever", "Chronic alcohol-induced liver disease: possible but lacks acute decompensation pattern", "Gynecologic torsion: could be considered but systemic signs favor intra-abdominal pathology", "Ectopic pregnancy: possible due to sexual activity but contradicted by prior appropriate gonococcal treatment"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with tachycardia (suggestive of shock or sepsis)", "Recent unexplained weight loss", "Chronic heavy alcohol use", "Sexual activity without contraception"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Acute Process", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.219, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Systemic hypotension and fever reduce likelihood of isolated gynecologic pathology as primary explanation."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Obstruction", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.175, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of classic hepatic vein obstruction signs (ascites, encephalopathy) weakens this hypothesis despite systemic findings."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4736842105263159, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic alcohol use and weight loss increase suspicion for chronic pancreatitis-related biliary obstruction, but evidence remains limited."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3", "B3.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": 